                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8eb0d7b4-65b1-4b81-bb15-8be10f40ef95",
                        "entry_id": "1ae48cfb-f8da-3efe-8a12-88b6569434de",
                        "tags": [
                            "orthographe rectifiée de 1990"
                        ],
                        "form": "persifflage"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fd4c0e21-0146-340f-8338-e786bdde4b17",
                        "entry_id": "1ae48cfb-f8da-3efe-8a12-88b6569434de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Propos de celui ou celle qui persifle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "43c38dec-9476-47ef-9c08-5f8ab65b1179",
                                "sense_id": "fd4c0e21-0146-340f-8338-e786bdde4b17",
                                "text": "Il était visible que chaque parole, chaque geste et surtout les continuelles et parfois gauches attentions de son mari l'agaçaient ; elle y répondait par une attitude hostile et méprisante, s'efforçant de la cacher sous un ton d'ironie familière et de persiflage affectueux […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce384292-0992-4372-820b-175da04a257f",
                                "sense_id": "fd4c0e21-0146-340f-8338-e786bdde4b17",
                                "text": "C'est l'apogée pour Dupatoy : sur le cadavre, il prononce un éloge funèbre dans lequel, tout en notant avec indulgence les erreurs et l'excessive audace de \" son jeune ami \" tombé, il rend hommage à la pureté de ses intentions stériles. Cet abject persiflage lui concilie définitivement les plus rebelles. La révolution est défaite."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4bfd4b17-7a4a-4695-94fc-0bcac274910c",
                                "sense_id": "fd4c0e21-0146-340f-8338-e786bdde4b17",
                                "text": "Exaspéré par tout ce qu’on s’ingéniait à inventer contre lui, Roukoz finit par réagir d’une manière si bouffonne qu’elle lui fit certainement plus de tort que tous les persiflages de ses détracteurs."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9369fbdb-35c6-4d3a-9bb2-7f592e5a74a6",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ae48cfb-f8da-3efe-8a12-88b6569434de",
                        "source_sense_id": "fd4c0e21-0146-340f-8338-e786bdde4b17",
                        "target_lang_word": "mockery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mockery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e920c68a-e305-30b7-9d07-5788c5e24789",
                                        "entry_id": "ad3455c8-c004-3f57-bb11-032792378422",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The action of mocking; ridicule, derision."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea2c3bbb-a6a8-3d14-af32-a2c5207c75e8",
                                        "entry_id": "ad3455c8-c004-3f57-bb11-032792378422",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something so lacking in necessary qualities as to inspire ridicule; a laughing-stock."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "50515d62-716b-337d-ab9d-ae02811ea3d1",
                                        "entry_id": "ad3455c8-c004-3f57-bb11-032792378422",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something insultingly imitative; an offensively futile action, gesture etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "457811ef-5576-3747-a012-a6b75acabad7",
                                        "entry_id": "ad3455c8-c004-3f57-bb11-032792378422",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mimicry, imitation, now usually in a derogatory sense; a travesty, a ridiculous simulacrum."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "072bb6f6-e5f5-4da9-83d5-5c9b315fc6fd",
                                                "sense_id": "457811ef-5576-3747-a012-a6b75acabad7",
                                                "text": "The defendant wasn't allowed to speak at his own trial - it was a mockery of justice."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7350b5db-0c6a-43be-8c96-cefdce043436",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ae48cfb-f8da-3efe-8a12-88b6569434de",
                        "source_sense_id": "fd4c0e21-0146-340f-8338-e786bdde4b17",
                        "target_lang_word": "ridicule",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ridicule",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "049061f5-5f83-3ce0-a9fb-b48fd87b49d6",
                                        "entry_id": "28df4ad0-1091-3bd5-af20-ffe8870f8304",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To criticize or disapprove of someone or something through scornful jocularity; to make fun of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc266c04-bc54-4689-9fea-dea177a96e94",
                                                "sense_id": "049061f5-5f83-3ce0-a9fb-b48fd87b49d6",
                                                "text": "His older sibling constantly ridiculed him with sarcastic remarks."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ridicule",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6950807-a90e-3621-bf8f-6b4cdd91f079",
                                        "entry_id": "362abcb8-b48e-37d2-8cfe-fa43638e2786",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Derision; mocking or humiliating words or behavior."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1efcd616-ce29-4310-9e76-b017d405adb3",
                                                "sense_id": "d6950807-a90e-3621-bf8f-6b4cdd91f079",
                                                "text": "Safe from the Bar, the Pulpit, and the Throne, / Yet touch'd and sham'd by Ridicule alone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a94583b-5428-4175-8349-55243f0e950f",
                                                "sense_id": "d6950807-a90e-3621-bf8f-6b4cdd91f079",
                                                "text": "When he was young you'd not find him doing well in school,\nHis mind would turn unto the waters.\nAlways the focus of adolescent ridicule,\nHe has no time for farmer's daughters.\nAlienated from the clique society,\nA lonely boy finds peace in fishing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "385611c9-0567-3b11-8fb5-d687fd72d5e0",
                                        "entry_id": "362abcb8-b48e-37d2-8cfe-fa43638e2786",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An object of sport or laughter; a laughing stock."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "baeb650d-0194-4733-b6d6-724ee7f04a2d",
                                                "sense_id": "385611c9-0567-3b11-8fb5-d687fd72d5e0",
                                                "text": "[Marlborough] was so miserably ignorant, that his deficiencies made him the ridicule of his contemporaries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7507228a-75eb-45b5-9134-957a0c3a3309",
                                                "sense_id": "385611c9-0567-3b11-8fb5-d687fd72d5e0",
                                                "text": "To the people […] but a trifle, to the king but a ridicule."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5d38bc52-fff7-3c07-b7b1-2a2a486fde8c",
                                        "entry_id": "362abcb8-b48e-37d2-8cfe-fa43638e2786",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being ridiculous; ridiculousness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbfcdc9c-8086-4424-96a2-2f10caddbd3a",
                                                "sense_id": "5d38bc52-fff7-3c07-b7b1-2a2a486fde8c",
                                                "text": "to see the ridicule of this monstrous practice"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da56acbd-4ea2-4024-bf1d-ce4256c1d959",
                                                "sense_id": "5d38bc52-fff7-3c07-b7b1-2a2a486fde8c",
                                                "text": "More keenly alive perhaps than any of her sisters to the little ridicules that belonged to Mrs. Palmer's character, she yet saw how small was their importance, and that Mrs. Palmer was not only a better but a happier person than most of those with whom she was acquainted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ridicule",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71881fa9-8b55-370a-a6ce-7268e2bcb22b",
                                        "entry_id": "4adbab0f-37a0-3456-939d-8e816fe116c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "ridiculous"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9271cf85-10c4-485c-94f7-7da66f684784",
                                                "sense_id": "71881fa9-8b55-370a-a6ce-7268e2bcb22b",
                                                "text": "late 17th century, John Aubrey, Brief Lives\nThis action […] became so ridicule."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ridicule",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b501afd-7146-3d88-b504-c74f6947b536",
                                        "entry_id": "ddfbffbb-e6d8-36df-8484-e42e2f208a17",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small woman's handbag; a reticule."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical",
                                            "regional"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a90d4e90-5449-4014-8bc8-e33a28633f61",
                                                "sense_id": "5b501afd-7146-3d88-b504-c74f6947b536",
                                                "text": "[…] while paying her own compliments to Mrs. Bates, and appearing to attend to the good old lady’s replies, she saw her with a sort of anxious parade of mystery fold up a letter which she had apparently been reading aloud to Miss Fairfax, and return it into the purple and gold ridicule by her side, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "864c67dd-3c08-4a11-a71c-34c1a233300e",
                                                "sense_id": "5b501afd-7146-3d88-b504-c74f6947b536",
                                                "text": "I hastily drew my empty hand from my Ridicule."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "606b879c-df5e-4a5d-8a9a-8bea566f0f93",
                                                "sense_id": "5b501afd-7146-3d88-b504-c74f6947b536",
                                                "text": "“Tills be blowed!” said Mr. Claypole; “there’s more things besides tills to be emptied.” “What do you mean?” asked his companion. “Pockets, women’s ridicules, houses, mailcoaches, banks,” said Mr. Claypole, rising with the porter."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
